                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_53\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit removes an `if (sourceTrack != null) { ... }` guard around the\nretargeting of a bone track and instead makes `retargetTrack` handle a null\n`sourceTrack` internally by falling back to a single-keyframe \"bind pose\"\ntrack. Before the fix, whenever a target bone's mapped source bone had no\nanimation track (`sourceTrack == null`), the code simply skipped adding any\ntrack for that bone at all \u2014 this is the \"retargeting logic error\" described\nin the fix commit message.\n\nTracing the history of `Util.retargetAnimation`/`retargetTrack`:\n\n- candidate_36 first introduces `retargetTrack`, but at that point the\n  `sourceTrack` lookup (`MyAnimation.findTrack`) happens *inside*\n  `retargetTrack` itself and is used unconditionally\n  (`sourceTrack.getTimes()`), with no null check anywhere. A null source\n  track would simply cause a `NullPointerException`, not the \"skip the bone\"\n  logic error being fixed.\n\n- candidate_40 only removes an unrelated `twist` parameter from the same\n  methods; it does not touch null handling.\n\n- candidate_53 refactors the call site to look up `sourceTrack` in\n  `retargetAnimation` (via `MyAnimation.findTrack`) and pass it into\n  `retargetTrack`, and \u2014 critically \u2014 wraps the track-creation/`addTrack`\n  call in a brand-new `if (sourceTrack != null) { ... }` guard, while also\n  adding `Validate.nonNull(sourceTrack, \"source track\")` inside\n  `retargetTrack`. This is exactly the buggy \"skip bones with no source\n  track\" behavior that the fix commit later removes.\n\n- candidate_54 only adds an explanatory comment\n  (`// handle null sourceTrack`) to the same `if` statement introduced in\n  candidate_53, with no functional change.\n\n- candidate_55 is essentially identical to the fix commit itself (removing\n  the guard and adding bind-pose fallback logic), so it is the fix, not the\n  bug introduction.\n\nSince candidate_53 is the first commit to introduce the specific\n\"silently skip bones whose source track is null\" logic that the fix commit\ncorrects, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
